  "answer_core": "Do not pick a dissertation direction yet. Treat the next couple of weeks as a short probe, not a commitment. The decision hinges on two gates: whether the Silva path is real and finishable, and whether your current fallback remains fully viable.\n\nFirst, talk to your advisor before involving anyone else. Confirm what support they would give if you tested the Silva direction, and what resources remain available if you stay with the fallback. Then do a focused, time‑boxed check with Dr. Silva: what data actually exists, who controls it, when you could inspect it, what collaboration and authorship terms look like, and which pieces would be clearly yours.\n\nIn parallel, verify that the fallback can still carry a dissertation if the Silva path fails. That means confirming advisor backing, resources, access, and a clear stop‑loss date that lets you safely return.\n\nMake the real choice only after both gates have concrete evidence. Keep the sequence clean: advisor → short data/access probe → committee only once you know whether the Silva path is real and whether the fallback remains protected.",
